 "result": "I created two files. I couldn't build or run the image here, so neither has been tested.\n\n- **`Dockerfile`**: a three-stage build on `node:20-alpine`.\n  1. The first stage installs the frontend dependencies and runs `npm run build` to produce `frontend/build`.\n  2. The second stage installs the backend's production dependencies with `npm ci --omit=dev`.\n  3. The final stage copies in `server.js`, `src/`, `customQuotes/` and the built frontend. It sets `NODE_ENV=PRODUCTION` so Express serves the frontend, runs as the unprivileged `node` user, and listens on port 3002 (`PORT` can override it).\n- **`.dockerignore`**: leaves out `node_modules`, build output, `.git`, docs, assets and `.env`.\n\nI left `.env` out of the image on purpose, so secrets aren't baked in. You pass `PORT`, `SERVICE_URL` and `UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY` at runtime instead. For example: `docker run --env-file .env -p 3002:3002 <image>`.\n\nI didn't use `npm start` or `server_bootup.sh`. Both reinstall dependencies and rebuild the frontend at startup, which the multi-stage build already does.",
